{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Tzaneh</b> — He mentioned sheep and cattle, because he needs them for food and clothing more than riding horses and donkeys. Then he mentioned beasts of the field and <i>shedei</i>, like <i>sadeh</i> (field), in the way of <i>kol atzilei yadav</i>." "<b>And the word <i>behemot</i></b> — is inclusive, unlike what Yefet said: for the <i>behemah</i> is that which eats grass. And behold, what will he do: <i>l-yish gever be-vehemah</i>?!"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes one word from Psalms 8:8 (וצנה) as the lemma; this is the Aramaic word for sheep appearing in Targum. The phrase כל אצילי ידי appears to be a truncated citation, possibly from Targum or liturgical usage; rendered literally without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:42.250311711Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}